Overlay patch 0038: full right-stick C-pad on the gamepad (device round 2).

SF64's upstream default (Engine.cpp) binds the right stick to only TWO of the
four C-buttons: UP->C-up (RIGHTY-) and RIGHT->C-right (RIGHTX+). C-down and
C-left live on the triggers and the B/Y face buttons, NOT the stick — so on a
physical controller pushing the right stick down or left does nothing ("only
joystick right and up do anything"), and the game's "hit C-down!" prompts are
unreachable by the stick. Make the right stick a full 4-way C-pad.

Two edits, because LUS only applies game defaults to a controller that has NO
saved config (ControlDeck::Init -> HasConfig ? ReloadAllMappingsFromConfig :
AddDefaultMappings). An existing install has saved config, so a default change
alone never reaches it.

1. Engine.cpp default: add RIGHTX- -> C-left and RIGHTY+ -> C-down alongside the
   existing trigger bindings (kept as alternates). Fresh installs, and anyone
   who does "Reset controller to defaults", get the full C-pad.

2. os.cpp one-time migration: right after the deck loads persisted config
   (osContInit), add the same two SDL axis-direction mappings to port 1's
   C-down / C-left buttons if a one-shot CVar guard is unset. The mapping IDs
   are deterministic (P-B-SDLA-AD) so AddButtonMapping is idempotent; the guard
   (gSohIos.CPadFull) means a user who later deletes a binding keeps it deleted.

__IOS__-guarded (the migration is an iOS/visionOS device-feedback fix; the
oracle keeps upstream behavior). Engine.cpp default change is unconditional —
it is the game's intended default and harmless on desktop.


--- a/libultraship/src/public/libultra/os.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/public/libultra/os.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@
 #include "libultraship/libultraship.h"
 #include <SDL2/SDL.h>
 #include <ratio>
+#ifdef __IOS__
+#include "controller/controldevice/controller/mapping/sdl/SDLAxisDirectionToButtonMapping.h"
+#include "public/bridge/consolevariablebridge.h"
+#endif
 
 // Establish a chrono duration for the N64 46.875MHz clock rate
 typedef std::ratio<3000, 64> n64ClockRatio;
@@ -31,6 +35,43 @@
 
     Ship::Context::GetInstance()->GetControlDeck()->Init(controllerBits);
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0038, device round 2): the game default binds only
+    // right-stick UP->C-up and RIGHT->C-right; DOWN and LEFT are on the
+    // triggers/face buttons, so on a gamepad the right stick is only half a
+    // C-pad ("only up and right do anything"). Add DOWN->C-down and
+    // LEFT->C-left once, here — right after the deck loads persisted config, so
+    // it reaches EXISTING installs (Init only applies game defaults when there
+    // is NO saved config, so changing the default alone never does). Mapping
+    // IDs are deterministic -> AddButtonMapping is idempotent; the CVar guard
+    // lets a later user removal stick.
+    if (!CVarGetInteger("gSohIos.CPadFull", 0)) {
+        auto sohCtrl = Ship::Context::GetInstance()->GetControlDeck()->GetControllerByPort(0);
+        if (sohCtrl != nullptr) {
+            const struct {
+                CONTROLLERBUTTONS_T btn;
+                int32_t axis;
+                int32_t dir;
+            } sohCPad[] = {
+                { BTN_CDOWN, SDL_CONTROLLER_AXIS_RIGHTY, 1 },
+                { BTN_CLEFT, SDL_CONTROLLER_AXIS_RIGHTX, -1 },
+            };
+            for (const auto& sohM : sohCPad) {
+                auto sohBtn = sohCtrl->GetButton(sohM.btn);
+                if (sohBtn != nullptr) {
+                    auto sohMap =
+                        std::make_shared<Ship::SDLAxisDirectionToButtonMapping>(0, sohM.btn, sohM.axis, sohM.dir);
+                    sohBtn->AddButtonMapping(sohMap);
+                    sohMap->SaveToConfig();
+                    sohBtn->SaveButtonMappingIdsToConfig();
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        CVarSetInteger("gSohIos.CPadFull", 1);
+        CVarSave();
+    }
+#endif
+
     return 0;
 }
 
